.TH mbnavadjust-qt 1 "10 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbnavadjust-qt\fP \- Interactive adjustment of the navigation of swath sonar surveys, using the bathymetry where the surveys overlap.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbnavadjust-qt\fP
.br
[--input=project {-Iproject}
.br
--reset-crossings {-R}
.br
--dark-background {-D}
.br
--verbose {-V}
.br
--help {-H}
.br
--dump
.br
--replay=script
.br
--export=prefix
.br
--crossing=number]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbnavadjust-qt\fP is the Qt6 version of \fBmbnavadjust\fP. It reads and writes the same project files and runs
the same project code as \fBmbnavadjust\fP, so the two programs can be used on one project, one after the other.
The project is a *.nvh file with a directory *.dir beside it.

The window holds the project status and the list of the project, the crossing being analyzed, the messages and,
when it is shown, the model plot. These are docks that can be moved, or floated out of the window. The lists are
tables: a click on a column header sorts the table.

Clicking a section, crossing or tie in the list loads it in the crossing editor. A click on a survey, block, file or
reference grid selects it. In the crossing editor the left mouse button drags the second section over the first, the
middle mouse button (or Alt with the left button) drags out a box to zoom, and the right mouse button picks the
navigation points nearest the mouse for the tie. A click in the misfit or vertical misfit plot sets the working offset.

In the model plot the left mouse button picks a tie, the middle button picks an untied crossing, or a block in
the Tie Offsets plot, and the right button drags out the range to zoom.

Auto-Pick, Invert Navigation, Update Grids and the other long steps run in the background, and the window stays
alive while they run. Edit > Undo takes back the tie edits and status changes made by hand; it does not take back the
long steps.

The project is written after every 10 tie edits, at once for status changes and for Apply in the Controls form, and when the
project or the window is closed. Closing does not ask: the edits are written.

The map of \fBmbnavadjust\fP (Visualize Survey) is not yet available in this program.

