.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-input=\fIproject\fP {\-I\fIproject\fP}
Opens this project (a *.nvh file) at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-reset-crossings {\-R}
Resets the crossings of the project when it is opened.
.TP
.B \-\-dark-background {\-D}
Draws the plots white on black. Without this option the plots follow the light or dark setting of the system.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose {\-V}
Writes more information to the standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-help {\-H}
Prints the usage and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-dump
With \-\-input: prints what each list shows, without a window.
.TP
.B \-\-replay=\fIscript\fP
Runs the user actions in a text file, without a window, and prints what the program shows. Used to compare the program with \fBmbnavadjust\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-export=\fIprefix\fP
With \-\-input: writes the plots as PNG files named after the prefix, without a window.
.TP
.B \-\-crossing=\fInumber\fP
With \-\-export: the crossing to show. The default is the first crossing.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmbnavadjust\fP(1), \fBmbnavadjustmerge\fP(1), \fBmbsystem\fP(1), \fBmbgrid\fP(1)

.SH BUGS
A project can be open in one program at a time; nothing prevents two programs from opening the same project at once.
